<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balaguer</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balaguer is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segre">Segre</a> in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a>, Catalonia. Taken from the Muslims by Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ermengol-vi-of-urgell">Ermengol VI of Urgell</a> in 1105, it became the capital of the county of Urgell. In 1413 Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-urgell">James II of Urgell</a>, the defeated claimant to the Aragonese throne, was besieged there by Ferdinand I and forced to surrender.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balaguer.jpg" alt="Balaguer" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ainhoa from Catalunya · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santa_Maria_de_Balaguer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
